Independent learners continue developing skills after formal education ends; a 2022 study found adults with strong critical thinking skills were 40% more likely to engage in professional development throughout their careers.
Media literacy education, a subset of critical thinking, has been shown to reduce susceptibility to misinformation by 20–30% in RCTs conducted across Europe.
Self-directed learning produces better long-term retention than passive instruction — the act of questioning and evaluating information encodes it more deeply than rote memorisation.
